From 9797fb112c2b06026277b37fe10863c6afb46c83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshkamdar67 <harshkamdar67@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:52:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 12/32] ggml, vulkan: fused Inkling 2 relative-position
 attention mask

GGML_OP_INKLING_REL_MASK writes the per-head flash attention mask in one pass: each
workgroup builds one (head, token) bias row over all distances in shared memory, then
writes mask + row[rel_pos] - sink for every key in F16. It replaces the bias table product,
sink subtraction, two transposing copies, the gather, the mask add and the F16 cast.
B60: pp512 992 -> 1049, pp2048 913 -> 1030, pp512 at 32K depth 513 -> 733 tok/s; decode
35.8 -> 37.1; wikitext-2 PPL 7.6919 -> 7.6851.
